course: dictionary
lesson: 120
title: Adorer
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: An adorer is a person who loves or admires someone or something very much. The ending -er often means a person who does something, so an adorer is one who adores.
explain: Most people today say «fan» or «admirer» instead. Adorer is a rarer word that you will meet mostly in stories, poems and old books. When you see it, use the nearby words to check what it means.
explain: Long ago, an adorer could also be someone who worships, especially in a church. A poem might describe «the adorers kneeling quietly before the altar». The setting tells you they are worshippers, not just fans.
fact: Adorer is a noun. One is an adorer, and more than one is adorers.
fact: «Adorer» means someone who loves or admires someone or something very much.
fact: In old church use, an adorer is someone who worships.
fact: Today people more often say «fan» or «admirer».
fact: In French, adorer is a verb meaning to love. «J'aime le pain» means I like bread, and after aimer, adorer, détester and préférer you use le, la, l' or les for things in general. This is French grammar, not English.
exercise: What does adorer mean? | A loud bell in a church tower | *Someone who loves or admires someone very much | Someone who sells flowers | A kind of old wooden boat
exercise: Which everyday word means nearly the same as adorer? | *Fan | Stone | Whistle | Gloomy
exercise: Which word is the plural of adorer? | *adorers | adore | adorer's | adoring
test: In an old poem, «the adorers knelt quietly before the statue». What is the best meaning here? | People who were lost in the hills | *People who love or worship the statue | People who sold the statue | People who hate statues
test: Why do most people today say «fan» instead of adorer? | Adorer is brand new slang | Fan is the only word that means worship | *Adorer is rare and old-fashioned, found mostly in stories and poems | Adorer means something bad and rude
exam: A child says, «My little sister is my biggest adorer.» What does the child mean? | Her sister works as a church helper | *Her sister loves and admires her very much | Her sister is a famous singer | Her sister is always angry with her
